# Components

Rules for files under `app/components/`. Follow global rules in `global.mdc`.

## Current starter

`app/components/` is empty and kept with `.gitkeep`. Add a component when the same UI is used in more than one page. Leave one-off markup in the page.

## Location

```
app/components/
├── NoDataCard.vue
└── modals/
    └── EditItem.vue
```

- Modals go in `modals/`.
- Group a growing set in a feature folder (`devices/`).
- Use **PascalCase** filenames (`NoDataCard.vue`).

Nuxt auto-registers components. Import explicitly when that makes the page easier to read:

```ts
import NoDataCard from '~/components/NoDataCard.vue'
```

## File shape

```vue
<template>
  <!-- markup -->
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
// imports → props/emits → state → composables → handlers
</script>

<style scoped></style>
```

- One `<script setup lang="ts">` block.
- Scoped styles only when the component needs CSS that does not belong in `assets/styles/components/`.

## Props and emits

Type props and emits. Default optional props with `withDefaults`.

```ts
interface NoDataCardProps {
  title?: string
  description?: string
}

const props = withDefaults(defineProps<NoDataCardProps>(), {
  title: 'Nothing here',
  description: '',
})

const emit = defineEmits<{
  retry: []
}>()
```

Two-way visibility uses `update:isVisible`:

```ts
const emit = defineEmits<{
  'update:isVisible': [value: boolean]
  save: [payload: ItemUpdatePayload]
}>()
```

- Emit domain events (`save`). Do not mutate the parent's object in place.
- The parent or a composable performs the API call.

## What belongs here

- Empty states, result panels, and dialogs reused by several routes.
- Buttons that repeat the same confirm-and-mutate flow.
- Smaller components composed inside larger ones.

## What does not belong here

- App chrome (use `app/layouts/`).
- `definePageMeta` or middleware.
- Markup used by a single page.
- Direct HTTP calls. Use a composable.
- A second script block or the Options API.

## Adding a component

1. Confirm the UI is duplicated or is a modal/dialog.
2. Choose `app/components/` or a subfolder.
3. Type props and emits.
4. Pass data in as props. Call composables only when the component owns the action.
5. Remove `.gitkeep` once the folder has a real file if git no longer needs it. Nested empty folders still need `.gitkeep`.
